-   `turbulence.stdio` is the deliberately minimal component this track created, and parasite's
-   closure is 37 modules, so moving `Mutex` would undo most of what splitting the standard
-   streams off achieved. `Counter` had no users inside rudiments or out — the only other
-   `Counter` in the tree is `ultimatum.Reckoning.Counter`, an unrelated nested enum — and
-   `Atomic[Int]` with `ere(_ + 1)` is `getAndIncrement`, so it was removed rather than re-homed.
+   `turbulence.stdio` est le composant délibérément minimal que ce chantier a créé, et la clôture
+   de parasite compte 37 modules : déplacer `Mutex` annulerait donc l'essentiel de ce qu'a apporté
+   la séparation des flux standard. `Counter` n'avait aucun utilisateur, ni dans rudiments ni
+   ailleurs — le seul autre `Counter` de l'arborescence est `ultimatum.Reckoning.Counter`, une
+   énumération imbriquée sans rapport — et `Atomic[Int]` avec `ere(_ + 1)` équivaut à
+   `getAndIncrement` : il a donc été supprimé plutôt que relocalisé.

-   So rudiments holds these utilities precisely *because* they are used from below the topics
-   they belong to. Re-homing them by subject means first moving their low-level consumers, which
-   is a much larger change than this item describes. The earlier measurement stands too: none of
-   these moves would shrink any closure.
